00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.040
A lot of the data that we
talk about in the day-to-day

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.160
is structured data.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.540
It's your advertising data.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.670
It's your CRM data.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.420
It's your structured
databases that you can either

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.990
access with a SQL
query or a dashboard,

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.900
but today we talk about
unstructured data.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.770
And what is unstructured data?

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.410
Unstructured data
is the type of data

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:30.070
that doesn't come with a
predefined or an intuitive

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.280
schema that is easy
understood by machines.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.150
So machines can display
it, like photos,

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.400
and you can browse through it.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.270
You can easily change
them, but the machine

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:40.520
will have a hard time telling
you what's in the photo.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:46.120
The same with recorded audio,
video, and email, for instance.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.250
It's all digital but
it's hard for the machine

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.280
to actually understand
what is in the email.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.680
So this is where the
big opportunity is.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.700
So if we know that half, 50%, of
organization's structured data

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.140
is actively used in
decision making--

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.840
this is a survey.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.640
This is probably on
the high end even

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.400
because if you ask people did
they look at data before making

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.740
a decision, a lot of people
are going to say yes.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:11.200
But how many people
actually did it?

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.120
That number goes
down to less than 1%

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.490
if it's about unstructured data.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:20.380
For instance, you can think of
older recordings of your call

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:21.070
center.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.355
