00:02:37.247 --> 00:02:39.330
This wouldn't be a Google
talk if we wouldn't talk

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.680
about AI and machine learning.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.760
And in this case, it really
signifies that bridge

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.340
between your unstructured
data and your structured data.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.230
So you probably already
have in place ways

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.290
to deal with your
structured data,

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.440
but machine learning really is
the bridge between those data

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.370
sources.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:00.690
And Google Cloud then is
really the opportunity for you

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:03.150
to leverage and
to use, but Google

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:06.798
has learned about data
in the last decade or so,

00:03:06.798 --> 00:03:09.090
developing their own algorithms,
and you can apply this

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:09.923
to your own dataset.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:14.260
So what is machine learning?

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.010
Well, everything is
illustrated by cat and the dog.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.980
Deep neural networks is a
form of machine learning,

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:24.820
and it basically trains to
recognize certain patterns

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.060
in unstructured data.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.270
In this case, it's a photo
and it tries to figure out

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.590
it's a laundry basket.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.790
Is that a cat or is that a dog?

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.630
So the animation on
the right signifies

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.490
different neural
[AUDIO OUT] different models

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.368
that the ML
application is trying

00:03:41.368 --> 00:03:42.410
to figure out what it is.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.202
And at the end it says,
OK, it's not a cat.

00:03:44.202 --> 00:03:45.700
It's a dog.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.410
This sounds simple,
but what if you

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.702
have to decide whether this
is a chihuahua or a muffin.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.530
If your model can
differentiate between these two

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.010
you are on the right way.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.980
Is it a labradoodle or
is it fried chicken?

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:03.290
Sheepdog or mop?

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:05.510
This really goes to
show how delicate some

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.700
